#message 3 "Prakash: \"Reyes. Assignment first, then the door.\""
#message 4 "Prakash: \"Corner Pharmacy on Main got hit overnight. Back door forced, a few boxes of prescription painkillers gone.\""
#message 5 "Prakash: \"It was called in by a delivery driver, Lenny Marsh, Harbor Express. He says he saw kids running from the place at eleven. His van is parked on Main Street. Check his story.\""
#message 6 "Prakash: \"Then document the scene. Photographs, and anything the burglar dropped. Here's the precinct camera and a report form. Don't lose either one. The camera is older than you are.\""
#message 7 "He slides a camera and a blank report form across the counter. You take them both."
#message 8 "Prakash: \"Go home, Reyes. Come back tomorrow and do it again.\""
#message 9 "Prakash: \"You made the arrest. Now write the report and file it with me. That's the part that puts him in front of a judge.\""
#message 10 "Prakash: \"Warehouse 7 on Pier Road. Radio for backup before you go near it. Bukowski will meet you there. Do not go in alone.\""
#message 11 "Prakash: \"Photos, a bottle and a statement. Take them to Records and see what we have on Harbor Express. Mrs. Ortiz filed a complaint about them last month.\""
#message 12 "Prakash: \"Lenny Marsh. Harbor Express van, Main Street. Check his story against his van before you believe a word of it. The details are on the board.\""
#message 13 "Prakash: \"So the driver's story has a hole in it. Good. Now the pharmacy. Photograph the damage, collect what you find and talk to Mrs. Ortiz.\""
#message 14 "The board holds a shift roster, a notice about the coffee fund and a flyer for a lost beagle named Chief. Your name is on the roster in pencil."
#message 15 "A new card is pinned up in Prakash's block capitals: CORNER PHARMACY B&E. REPORTED BY L. MARSH, HARBOR EXPRESS DRIVER, 11 PM. VAN PARKED MAIN ST. PHARMACIST: MRS. A. ORTIZ."
#message 16 "Sergeant Prakash has worked this desk for nineteen years. His mustache is regulation. His handwriting is not."
#message 17 "A long wooden counter. On it sit a desk radio, three wire trays and a brass nameplate: SGT. R. PRAKASH."
#message 18 "Three wire trays, labeled IN, OUT and FILED IN WRONG TRAY. The third one is the fullest."
#message 19 "The desk radio's call light blinks now and then. Dispatch runs everything through it. Your own radio is clipped to your shoulder."
#message 20 "Glass double doors with push bars. Main Street is on the other side."
#message 21 "A doorway with a small sign that reads RECORDS. The filing cabinets are back there."
#message 22 "Just past seven. The clock runs four minutes fast. Everyone knows and nobody fixes it."
#message 23 "A blue plaque with a gold star: MILLHAVEN POLICE DEPARTMENT."
#message 24 "Gray tile, green paint and humming lights."
#message 25 "Prakash glances at your badge. \"I know, Reyes. I signed for it.\""
#message 26 "Prakash: \"Hands out of my trays, Reyes.\""
#message 27 "You don't have a report form."
#message 28 "The report is already written. All eleven boxes."
#message 29 "You write the date and your badge number. The rest has to wait until there is an arrest to report."
#message 30 "You lean on the counter and fill in the report: the driver's story, the pharmacy scene, the ledger, the warehouse and the arrest. It takes eleven boxes and two pens."
#message 31 "Prakash: \"It's filed and it's in the system. Go home.\""
#message 32 "Prakash: \"A report with no arrest is a diary, Reyes. Finish the case first.\""
#message 33 "Prakash hands it back. \"It's blank. Write it first. The counter is right there.\""
#message 34 "Prakash flips through it. \"You mention a pill bottle. Where is it? Evidence goes in with the report.\""
#message 35 "Prakash: \"There are no photographs of the scene. Go back to the pharmacy and take them.\""
#message 36 "Prakash: \"You cite the driver's route sheet, but I don't see it. Attach it.\""
#message 37 "Prakash: \"Where's the ledger copy from Records? You can't quote a ledger you didn't bring.\""
#message 38 "Prakash: \"Mrs. Ortiz's statement isn't attached. Go get it.\""
#message 39 "Prakash reads every page. He checks the route sheet against the ledger, looks at the photographs and turns the bagged pill bottle over twice."
#message 40 "Prakash: \"Complete, signed and handed to me instead of a tray. Sorensen won't talk his way out of this. Nice work, Reyes.\""
#message 41 "He stamps the report and drops it in the OUT tray. The day shift is heading home. Your first case is closed, and so is your first shift."
#message 42 "You drop the report in the nearest tray. Without looking, Prakash fishes it out of FILED IN WRONG TRAY. \"Hand it to me, Reyes. That's what I'm here for.\""
#message 43 "Bud Bukowski is out on Main Street with the patrol car. You can probably hear him from here."
#message 44 "Prakash is busy. The desk radio is his, not yours."
